---

## Key Tasks Performed

### 1. Domain Controller Setup
- Installed Active Directory Domain Services (AD DS)
- Promoted server to Domain Controller
- Configured DNS and verified forward lookup zones
- Ensured DC used itself as DNS client

### 2. Network & DNS Troubleshooting
- Identified VM-to-VM connectivity failures due to NAT/Internal Network limitations
- Reconfigured environment to use Host-Only networking
- Corrected static IP and default gateway misconfigurations
- Diagnosed DNS timeouts caused by missing DNS client configuration
- Verified DNS resolution using `nslookup` and `ping`

### 3. User and Group Management
- Created Organizational Units (OUs) for logical separation
- Created domain users and security groups
- Assigned users to appropriate groups
- Verified user properties and login names via ADUC

### 4. Client Domain Join
- Joined Windows 11 workstation to the domain
- Authenticated using domain administrator credentials
- Verified domain membership post-reboot

### 5. User Authentication Validation
- Successfully logged into domain-joined workstation as:
CORP\J.Smith

- Confirmed domain authentication and profile creation

---

## Common Issues Encountered & Resolved

### Issue: Domain could not be found
- Root cause: Client DNS not pointing to Domain Controller
- Resolution: Corrected DNS settings and flushed resolver cache

### Issue: DNS timeouts from client
- Root cause: Missing DNS client configuration on DC01 and unstable VM network type
- Resolution: Set DC01 to use itself as DNS server and switched to Host-Only networking

